title: A redirect must not carry the session token to another host
updated: 2026-10-20T09:43:11Z
---

The user agent follows redirects and sends the session token along.

lib/WWW/Picnic.pm:130 builds the LWP::UserAgent without max_redirect => 0. The default of LWP is 7 redirects, and requests_redirectable covers GET and HEAD.

So a GET that answers 302 (get_cart, get_user, search, get_article) is followed, and the header X-Picnic-Auth (lib/WWW/Picnic.pm:346) goes to the redirect target. On the LWP of CPAN the header is not removed, so the foreign target holds the token of the logged in account, and its answer counts as the success of the call.

Decide: the user agent gets max_redirect => 0, and every 3xx is raised as an error with status, method and path.

Commit 570458e: Do not follow redirects, fail with a WWW::Picnic::Error (k7). Red proof: t/offline.t fails against the old lib (bbf2733) with 3 failed expectations (max_redirect 7 != 0, the error is no WWW::Picnic::Error, the message names no status, method and path), no die. Suite green: 4 files, 36 tests.

